<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One block of verse on one printed page: running head at the top with page number at the top right; the poem in stanzas, full width, with no marginal notes.</layout>
  <page_number>158</page_number>
  <running_head>ABRA. SACRIFICANS.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>Iudicra mentes fallere somnia.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>Non terret illum pauperies inops,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Nec inflat auri copia largior,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Aequam secundis rebus, &amp; asperis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Seruare mentem nouit, &amp; undique</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Vexationum si violentior</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Procella tentat, Tartarasi mouent</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Infesta turbas, impauidus manet.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Illum tuetur dextera Caelitum,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Certasque semper prouida semitas,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Monstrat, minaci nec sinit obrui</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Tentationum turbine grandium:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Si forte nutat, si pede lubricos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Quandoque calles ambigúo terit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Presssum periclis omnibus explicat.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" para="true">
      <i>Hac esse nostei sera satis docet.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Abramus: ex quo Patris Olympici</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Fidelis illum cura tegit, licet</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Multis petatur saepe malis, tamen</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Hac cuncta vincit maiorvatrocia.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Si damna crescunt, indomiti simul</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Augentur illi robora pectoris.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Natale quondam deserutt solum:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Fetuens coegit sollicitum fames Aegyptiorum littora visere.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Several words in the verse are blurred by stains and show-through; "Tartarasi", "nostei", "Abramus", "maiorvatrocia" and "Vexationum" are doubtful readings. "Presssum" and "deserutt" may be misprints. Greek-style ligatures "&amp;" kept as printed.</notes>
</page>
